							<div class="Section1"> <p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: center;" align="center"><font face="Garamond"><strong><span style="font-size: 24pt; font-family: Verdana; color: red;"><font face="Georgia" size="6">Officers</font><br /> </span></strong></font><span style="font-family: &quot;Arial Unicode MS&quot;;"><o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: center;" align="center">&nbsp;</p> <ul type="disc"><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">There is one officer for each of our “class channels”.&nbsp; The officer is responsible for making sure that each member of his/her class is following the guild rules, as well as attempting to answer any questions one might have about their class.&nbsp;There will be no more than 17 officers, not including alts of the guild leader/s.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">Each channel will have channel leaders, these are not officers, but should be treated respectfully.<span style="">&nbsp; </span>The channel leaders and officers are responsible for making sure that members of their channels understand and follow the guild rules.<span style="">&nbsp; </span>The channel officers will choose channel leaders.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">There are 6 counsel officers.<span style="">&nbsp; </span>These officers are there as support for the leaders, this is their primary function within the system.<span style="">&nbsp; </span>These are the officers that ideas regarding guild function should be brought to.<span style="">&nbsp; </span>Any idea that makes it past the counsel will be brought before the channel officers and finally to the guild.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">Class officers should try to meet with new members and get to know them a little bit, learn how they group and have fun with them!</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">Members on probation, including new members, cannot apply to become officers until their probationary period is over.&nbsp; </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">Officers are not to change the configuration of the guild website in any way without the express permission of the guild/site leader.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">Officers need to try to make themselves available. &nbsp;You are certainly not expected to leave a raid, group, ldon or other event, but you need to try to be available afterward.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">You are responsible for&nbsp;posting the raids in the motd and on the&nbsp;<a href="../forums/threadlist.aspx?fid=1163">Raids </a>Forum. &nbsp;Never schedule 2 guild events or raids for the same time.&nbsp; Check availability on the guild calendar and the Raids forum.&nbsp; If you need a&nbsp;raid planned&nbsp;post in the Raids Forum.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Guild manager public notes need to contain flags the character may have as well as the name of each character's main, if the member is a new member on probation, they’re joined date needs to be there as well.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Only the recruiting officer and guild leaders are to do guild invites.<span style="">&nbsp; </span>There may be exceptions to this these people are not available and ask another officer to do the invite.</span></strong></li></ul> <p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: red;">Current Officers:</span></strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></p> <p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: aquamarine;">Channel Officers</span></strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: aquamarine;">:</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></p> <ul type="disc"><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Mrhealer (Druids and Clerics) = </span></strong><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;"><a href="../player.aspx?pid=70350"><span style="font-weight: normal;">Luvena</span></a></span></strong><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; font-weight: normal;"><o:p></o:p></span></strong></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Mrpuller (Rangers and Monks) = </span></strong><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;"><a href="../player.aspx?pid=62755"><span style="font-weight: normal;">Noetikos</span></a></span></strong><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; font-weight: normal;"><o:p></o:p></span></strong></l